mke2fs compares the release uname() reports against kernel versions with
known ext2/ext4 limits (revision 0 file systems before 2.2, no block sizes
above 4096 before 2.6, metadata_csum advice before 3.18, no lazy inode
table init before 2.6.37).  On LikeOS that release is the LikeOS version
("0.2.9"), which would read as older than all of them and make mke2fs
create revision 0 file systems.  The checks take their non-applicable
branch, the one upstream builds for every other system.

